# Architecture

Protect boundaries: domain ownership, public contracts, persistence, tenancy, and process isolation. Do not leak storage models through public APIs.

Before a Type 1 choice, name at least two alternatives, the tradeoff, security impact, operational impact, and migration cost. Record it in `docs/templates/architecture-decision.md` when the choice will outlive the patch.

Prefer one coherent process until load, isolation, or team boundaries justify another. Kubernetes, extra queues, and new datastores need an operational reason, not a diagram.

Reversible internal structure stays local. Do not pause implementation for it.

If the approved architecture is wrong, stop the affected work and return to planning. Do not drift the design inside an implementation diff.
